[32m+[m[32m### 3. **SSL Certificate for Custom Domain 🔒**[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m#### **Option A: GitHub Pages (RECOMMENDED - Free & Automatic)**[m
[32m+[m[32mSince you want to move back to GitHub Pages:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m1. **Update DNS Settings** (with your domain registrar):[m
[32m+[m[32m   - Add these **A records**:[m
[32m+[m[32m     ```[m
[32m+[m[32m     185.199.108.153[m
[32m+[m[32m     185.199.109.153[m
[32m+[m[32m     185.199.110.153[m
[32m+[m[32m     185.199.111.153[m
[32m+[m[32m     ```[m
[32m+[m[32m   - OR add this **CNAME record**:[m
[32m+[m[32m     ```[m
[32m+[m[32m     abidhasan27.me → hasan2733.github.io[m
[32m+[m[32m     ```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m2. **Enable GitHub Pages:**[m
[32m+[m[32m   - Go to your GitHub repo settings[m
[32m+[m[32m   - Scroll to "Pages" section[m
[32m+[m[32m   - Select branch: `main` or `docs` (wherever your files are)[m
[32m+[m[32m   - Check "Enforce HTTPS" ✅[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m3. **GitHub will automatically:**[m
[32m+[m[32m   - Provision an SSL certificate (Let's Encrypt)[m
[32m+[m[32m   - Enable HTTPS[m
[32m+[m[32m   - Redirect HTTP to HTTPS[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m✅ **Result:** `https://abidhasan27.me` with free SSL[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m#### **Option B: Continue with Netlify (If you prefer)**[m
[32m+[m[32mNetlify also provides free SSL automatically:[m
[32m+[m[32m- Just keep your domain CNAME pointing to Netlify[m
[32m+[m[32m- SSL is automatic and free[m
[32m+[m[32m- Your form will work perfectly with FormSubmit too[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m#### **Option C: Cloudflare (Free Plan)**[m
[32m+[m[32mIf you want extra features like email forwarding:[m
[32m+[m[32m1. Sign up at cloudflare.com[m
[32m+[m[32m2. Add your domain[m
