[32m+[m[32m      <h1 class="blog-post__title">CSS Animations: Making Web Pages Alive</h1>[m
[32m+[m[32m      <div class="blog-post__meta">[m
[32m+[m[32m        <span>📅 November 8, 2024</span>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <span>⏱️ 7 min read</span>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <span>👤 Abid Hasan</span>[m
[32m+[m[32m      </div>[m
[32m+[m[32m    </div>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m    <div class="blog-post__content">[m
[32m+[m[32m      <h2>Why Animations Matter</h2>[m
[32m+[m[32m      <p>[m
[32m+[m[32m        CSS animations bring life to your web pages. They guide user attention, provide visual feedback, and create[m
[32m+[m[32m        memorable experiences. Best of all, you can create them entirely with CSS—no JavaScript needed![m
[32m+[m[32m      </p>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m      <h2>Basic CSS Animation Syntax</h2>[m
[32m+[m[32m      <p>[m
[32m+[m[32m        CSS animations use the <code>@keyframes</code> rule to define animation frames:[m
[32m+[m[32m      </p>[m
[32m+[m[32m      <pre><code>@keyframes slideIn {[m
[32m+[m[32m  0% {[m
[32m+[m[32m    transform: translateX(-100%);[m
[32m+[m[32m    opacity: 0;[m
[32m+[m[32m  }[m
[32m+[m[32m  100% {[m
[32m+[m[32m    transform: translateX(0);[m
[32m+[m[32m    opacity: 1;[m
[32m+[m[32m  }[m
[32m+[m[32m}[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m.element {[m
[32m+[m[32m  animation: slideIn 0.5s ease-out;[m
[32m+[m[32m}</code></pre>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m      <h2>Key Properties</h2>[m
[32m+[m[32m      <ul>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <li><strong>animation-name:</strong> Name of the @keyframes animation</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <li><strong>animation-duration:</strong> How long the animation takes</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <li><strong>animation-timing-function:</strong> ease, linear, ease-in, ease-out, ease-in-out</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <li><strong>animation-delay:</strong> Delay before animation starts</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <li><strong>animation-iteration-count:</strong> infinite or number of repetitions</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <li><strong>animation-direction:</strong> normal, reverse, alternate</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m      </ul>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m      <h2>Practical Examples</h2>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m      <h3>Example 1: Fade In Animation</h3>[m
[32m+[m[32m      <pre><code>@keyframes fadeIn {[m
[32m+[m[32m  from { opacity: 0; }[m
[32m+[m[32m  to { opacity: 1; }[m
[32m+[m[32m}[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m.card {[m
[32m+[m[32m  animation: fadeIn 1s ease-in;[m
[32m+[m[32m}</code></pre>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m      <h3>Example 2: Bounce Effect</h3>[m
[32m+[m[32m      <pre><code>@keyframes bounce {[m
[32m+[m[32m  0%, 100% { transform: translateY(0); }[m
[32m+[m[32m  50% { transform: translateY(-20px); }[m
[32m+[m[32m}[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m.button:hover {[m
[32m+[m[32m  animation: bounce 0.6s ease-in-out;[m
[32m+[m[32m}</code></pre>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m      <h3>Example 3: Gradient Shift</h3>[m
[32m+[m[32m      <pre><code>@keyframes gradientShift {[m
[32m+[m[32m  0% { background-position: 0% 50%; }[m
[32m+[m[32m  50% { background-position: 100% 50%; }[m
[32m+[m[32m  100% { background-position: 0% 50%; }[m
[32m+[m[32m}[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m.background {[m
[32m+[m[32m  background: linear-gradient(-45deg, #ee7752, #e73c7e);[m
[32m+[m[32m  background-size: 400% 400%;[m
[32m+[m[32m  animation: gradientShift 15s ease infinite;[m
[32m+[m[32m}</code></pre>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m      <h2>Performance Tips</h2>[m
[32m+[m[32m      <ul>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <li><strong>Use transform and opacity:</strong> They don't trigger layout reflows</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <li><strong>Avoid animating:</strong> width, height, left, right (these are slow)</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <li><strong>Use will-change:</strong> Hint to the browser for optimization</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <li><strong>Test on mobile:</strong> Ensure animations run smoothly</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m      </ul>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m      <h2>Conclusion</h2>[m
[32m+[m[32m      <p>[m
[32m+[m[32m        CSS animations are powerful tools for enhancing user experience. They're performant, accessible, and easy to[m
[32m+[m[32m        implement. Start with simple animations and build up to complex interactions. Your visitors will appreciate[m
[32m+[m[32m        the polish![m
[32m+[m[32m      </p>[m
