[32m+[m[32m    <div class="blog-post__header">[m
[32m+[m[32m      <h1 class="blog-post__title">Getting Started with GitHub Pages</h1>[m
[32m+[m[32m      <div class="blog-post__meta">[m
[32m+[m[32m        <span>📅 November 15, 2024</span>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <span>⏱️ 5 min read</span>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <span>👤 Abid Hasan</span>[m
[32m+[m[32m      </div>[m
[32m+[m[32m    </div>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m    <div class="blog-post__content">[m
[32m+[m[32m      <h2>What is GitHub Pages?</h2>[m
[32m+[m[32m      <p>[m
[32m+[m[32m        GitHub Pages is a free static site hosting service provided by GitHub. It's perfect for hosting your portfolio,[m
[32m+[m[32m        documentation, or any static website. You can deploy directly from your GitHub repository with zero configuration.[m
[32m+[m[32m      </p>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m      <h2>Why Use GitHub Pages?</h2>[m
[32m+[m[32m      <ul>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <li><strong>Free Hosting:</strong> No monthly fees or limitations</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <li><strong>Custom Domain Support:</strong> Use your own domain name</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <li><strong>SSL/HTTPS:</strong> Automatic HTTPS certificate</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <li><strong>Version Control:</strong> Built-in git version control</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <li><strong>Easy Deployment:</strong> Push to GitHub and your site goes live</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m      </ul>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m      <h2>Getting Started: Step by Step</h2>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m      <h3>Step 1: Create a Repository</h3>[m
[32m+[m[32m      <p>[m
[32m+[m[32m        First, create a new repository on GitHub. If you want your site at <code>username.github.io</code>, name your[m
[32m+[m[32m        repository exactly that. Otherwise, name it anything and your site will be at[m
[32m+[m[32m        <code>username.github.io/repository-name</code>.[m
[32m+[m[32m      </p>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m      <h3>Step 2: Enable GitHub Pages</h3>[m
[32m+[m[32m      <p>[m
[32m+[m[32m        Go to your repository settings, scroll down to the "Pages" section, and select which branch to deploy from[m
[32m+[m[32m        (usually <code>main</code> or <code>docs</code>).[m
[32m+[m[32m      </p>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m      <h3>Step 3: Create Your Content</h3>[m
[32m+[m[32m      <p>[m
[32m+[m[32m        Add an <code>index.html</code> file to your repository. This will be your homepage:[m
[32m+[m[32m      </p>[m
[32m+[m[32m      <pre><code>&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;[m
[32m+[m[32m&lt;html lang="en"&gt;[m
[32m+[m[32m&lt;head&gt;[m
[32m+[m[32m  &lt;meta charset="UTF-8"&gt;[m
[32m+[m[32m  &lt;title&gt;My Portfolio&lt;/title&gt;[m
[32m+[m[32m&lt;/head&gt;[m
[32m+[m[32m&lt;body&gt;[m
[32m+[m[32m  &lt;h1&gt;Hello, World!&lt;/h1&gt;[m
[32m+[m[32m  &lt;p&gt;Welcome to my portfolio.&lt;/p&gt;[m
[32m+[m[32m&lt;/body&gt;[m
[32m+[m[32m&lt;/html&gt;</code></pre>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m      <h3>Step 4: Add a Custom Domain</h3>[m
[32m+[m[32m      <p>[m
[32m+[m[32m        Create a <code>CNAME</code> file in your repository with your domain name:[m
[32m+[m[32m      </p>[m
[32m+[m[32m      <pre><code>yourdomain.com</code></pre>[m
[32m+[m[32m      <p>[m
[32m+[m[32m        Then, update your domain's DNS settings to point to GitHub Pages. Add these DNS records:[m
[32m+[m[32m      </p>[m
[32m+[m[32m      <ul>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <li><strong>A records:</strong> 185.199.108.153, 185.199.109.153, 185.199.110.153, 185.199.111.153</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <li><strong>CNAME record:</strong> username.github.io</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m      </ul>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m      <h2>Best Practices</h2>[m
[32m+[m[32m      <ul>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <li>Keep your HTML semantic and accessible</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <li>Use CSS for styling and responsive design</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <li>Optimize images for web performance</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <li>Make sure your site is mobile-friendly</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m        <li>Test your site before deploying</li>[m
[32m+[m[32m      </ul>[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m      <h2>Conclusion</h2>[m
[32m+[m[32m      <p>[m
[32m+[m[32m        GitHub Pages is an excellent choice for hosting your portfolio or static website. It's free, reliable, and[m
[32m+[m[32m        integrates seamlessly with your GitHub workflow. Start building today and show the world your projects![m
[32m+[m[32m      </p>[m
